"""Paper 2 data-response question sets.

Real 7132/2 papers have three compulsory questions of ~33 marks each (totals seen
2022-2024: 31-35), each built on its own context and appendices. Tariffs used here
match those in the live papers: 2-4 mark calculations, 3/4-mark 'explain',
6- and 9-mark 'analyse' and a 16-mark evaluation to finish each question.

Totals are 32, 33 or 34 so the mock builder can always combine three sets to
make exactly 100 marks (32+34+34 or 33+33+34).
"""


def T(title, headers, rows, note=""):
    return {"title": title, "headers": headers, "rows": rows, "note": note}


def Q(num, marks, kind, question, spec, **ms):
    d = {"num": num, "marks": marks, "kind": kind, "question": question, "spec": spec}
    d.update(ms)
    return d


